                <pb facs="0422" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7353b W 52/141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-07-03T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1923—11
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 12:51 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>264. Your 165, June 30, 2 p.m. The second paragraph of the offer mentioned
                    relates to all traffic originating in South Europe, i.e., the south to be served
                    by the Italian cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
